  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RECOVERY OF TIGERS AND THEIR PREY THROUGH SMART PATROL AND HABITAT IMPROVEMENT IN THAP LAN NATIONAL PARK, THAILAND, YEAR 2 - 4.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO (1) STRENGTHEN THE SPATIAL MONITORING AND REPORTING TOOL (SMART) PATROL SYSTEM IN THAP LAN THROUGH PARK RANGER TRAINING, MORALE BOOSTING SUPPORT, AND MONITORING PERFORMANCE (2) ENHANCE GRASS-BASED OPEN FOREST AREAS TO BOOST UNGULATE POPULATIONS IN THAP LAN BY USING HABITAT MANAGEMENT TOOLS (3) ESTIMATE THE DENSITY OF UNGULATES IN THE CORE AREA OF THAP LAN WITH DISTANCE PROGRAM SAMPLING TECHNIQUES AND (4) RENOVATE AN OLD RANGER STATION TO A FIELD WILDLIFE RESEARCH STATION FOR RESEARCHERS AND RANGER FIELD TEAMS.</narrative>
  </description>
